abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.3 tells the theory as one story: CORE.md starts from learning in
  a neural network, read as a network, and follows it in eight steps, from the
  ledger to the commons and to intelligence;
  formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean now audits 91 machine-checked results (44 in v22.2). New
  results cover the commons as the vortex of the whole, reciprocity and
  partner switching, discounting and the tragedy of the commons, the cost of
  listening, graded belief, connection against independence, care as a
  transfer, and power and distribution. Several claims are narrowed, and
  CORE.md now states how much each result says, which premises are assumed and
  which literatures each step sits next to. PREDICTIONS.md adds testing
  discipline and proposed tests of the health of intelligence and of the
  commons, a new line of concept notes with their research briefs, reports and
  reviews. DIALOGUE.md records how the author and an AI assistant build the
  model together. The release title uses "simulation of reality" to mean the
  internal model through which a system experiences and acts in the world, not
  a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal verification establishes
  implications under explicit premises; empirical, causal, political and
  normative interpretations remain open.
